WebOS kernel sources
======================

This is the upstream Linux LTS tree with the WebOS patch series applied.
The series is not stored in the repository; it is resolved and hashed by
`kernel/fetch-patches.sh` at build time.  See `kernel/patchset.conf` for the
list and `kernel/README.md` for the rationale.

The WebOS config fragment is installed next to this file as
`webos-fragment.config`.  It is a *fragment*, not a full config: it is applied
on top of upstream `defconfig`.

Building by hand
----------------

    cd /usr/src/linux-6.12.0
    make defconfig
    scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m .config webos-fragment.config
    make olddefconfig
    make -j"$(nproc)" bzImage modules
    make modules_install
    cp arch/x86/boot/bzImage /boot/vmlinuz-$(make -s kernelrelease)
    dracut --force --kver $(make -s kernelrelease)

Installing the `sys-kernel/webos-kernel` package does all of the above for you,
and is the supported path.
